{#- unsubscribe.html.j2 — /unsubscribe.html, the public bilingual unsubscribe page (SEE W4).

   Rendered by scripts.build_site.build_unsubscribe_page. Pure static page: nothing here
   reaches the network at build time; the button talks to POST /api/email/unsubscribe
   (app/unsubscribe.py) at run time.

   PUBLIC BY CONSTRUCTION, and for a harder reason than /support.html: someone who wants
   our marketing email to stop must never be asked to sign in first. Authorisation is the
   signed HMAC token in ?t= — no session, no account, no lookup.

   NOTHING MUTATES ON LOAD. Corporate mail scanners and link-preview bots fetch every URL
   in an inbound message; a page that unsubscribed on GET would silently opt out people
   who never clicked. The page renders inert and the reader presses the button. That is
   why "Nothing changes until you press it" is on screen — it is a true statement about
   the implementation, not reassurance copy.

   Visual idiom is /support.html's, deliberately: same shell, same rail, same mono
   micro-label, same footer, all resolved from theme.css tokens (mockups/support_email/
   PIN.md). No new palette or type decisions are taken here.

   STATE COLOUR LAW (PIN §1.1 — do not "simplify"):
     success = var(--ok)   error = var(--act)
   NEVER --up / --down: those are PRICE-DIRECTION tokens and theme.css swaps them under
   html[data-lang="zh"] for the Asia red-up convention, so a success panel painted with
   --up turns RED for every Chinese reader. --ok/--act encode health, never direction.

   Bilingual EN/ZH through the house t() macro (dual l-en/l-zh spans; theme.css hides the
   wrong one off html[data-lang]). No translated text in title= (CI-guarded). -#}
{% macro t(en, zh='') -%}
<span class="l-en">{{ en|safe }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ (zh if zh else en)|safe }}</span>
{%- endmacro %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-unsub="ready">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Unsubscribe — MastermindX</title>
{% set seo_title = "Unsubscribe — MastermindX" %}{% set seo_desc = "Turn off marketing email from MastermindX. Account emails — receipts, sign-in links and support replies — are unaffected." %}{% set seo_path = "unsubscribe.html" %}
{% include "_seo_head.html.j2" %}
{#- Public to REACH, not a page to index: it is reached only from a link in an email and
    only works with a signed token, so a tokenless search result would be a dead end for
    anyone who found it. Mirrored in lib/seo.py _EXCLUDE_NAMES, which keeps it out of
    sitemap.xml — both are needed, since a sitemap omission alone does not stop a crawl. -#}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<script>try{var th=localStorage.getItem('theme');if(th)document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme',th);var l=localStorage.getItem('lang')||(function(){try{var L=navigator.languages||[navigator.language||navigator.userLanguage||''],i;for(i=0;i<L.length;i++)if((L[i]||'').toLowerCase().slice(0,2)==='zh')return'zh';if(/Shanghai|Hong_Kong|Macau|Urumqi|Chongqing|Harbin|Kashgar|Chungking/.test(Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone||''))return'zh';}catch(e){}return'';})();if(l)document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-lang',l);}catch(e){}</script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="theme.css">
<style>
/* ── /unsubscribe.html page CSS. Same tokens, same recipes and the same two page-local
   additions as /support.html (PIN.md §1) — this is one surface in two rooms, so nothing
   is re-tasted here. Single column: the page has exactly one thing to do. ──────────── */
*{ box-sizing:border-box; }
body{ margin:0; padding-top:18px;            /* 18px top gap — house law */
  background:var(--bg); color:var(--text); font:14.5px/1.55 var(--font-ui);
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased; }
a{ color:var(--link); text-decoration:none; }

:root{
  --surface:color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 96%, var(--text));
  --brand-a:#3b82f6; --brand-b:#6366f1; --brand-c:#7c5cff;
}
html[data-theme="light"]{ --surface:color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 97%, #000); }

/* mono micro-label — the page's type signature, same as /support.html */
.mlab{ display:block; font:600 10.5px/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em;
  text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--muted); }
/* CJK: the mono stack carries no Hanzi, so a ZH label otherwise falls through to
   whatever the system picks — on some machines a SERIF. Pin a sans CJK face ahead of
   the mono chain and drop the wide Latin tracking, which reads as broken spacing. */
html[data-lang="zh"] .mlab{ font-family:"PingFang SC","Hiragino Sans GB",
  "Microsoft YaHei","Noto Sans CJK SC",var(--font-mono); letter-spacing:.04em; }
html[data-lang="zh"] .hero .eyebrow{ letter-spacing:.08em; }

/* ── shell ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.wrap{ max-width:620px; margin:0 auto; padding:20px 18px 64px; }
@media (min-width:900px){ .wrap{ padding:28px 26px 88px; } }

/* ── hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.hero{ text-align:center; padding:22px 6px 6px; }
.hero .eyebrow{ font:600 11px/1 var(--font-ui); letter-spacing:.18em; text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--muted); display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; margin-bottom:15px; }
.hero .eyebrow::before,.hero .eyebrow::after{ content:""; width:26px; height:1px;
  background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,var(--line)); }
.hero .eyebrow::after{ background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--line),transparent); }
.hero h1{ font:700 clamp(27px,4.6vw,38px)/1.08 var(--font-ui); letter-spacing:-.025em;
  margin:0 auto; max-width:20ch; }
/* inline-block keeps the second beat whole, so the headline breaks at the sentence */
.hero h1 .accent{ display:inline-block;
  background:linear-gradient(100deg,var(--brand-a),var(--brand-c));
  -webkit-background-clip:text; background-clip:text; -webkit-text-fill-color:transparent; }
.hero .sub{ font-size:clamp(14.5px,2.2vw,16px); color:var(--muted); max-width:50ch;
  margin:15px auto 0; line-height:1.5; }

/* ── the panel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.panel{ position:relative; border:1px solid var(--glass-brd); border-radius:16px;
  background:var(--surface); box-shadow:var(--card-shadow); overflow:hidden; margin-top:28px; }
/* the routing rail — 3px accent edge; --ok once the choice is recorded, --act when the
   link is dead or the write failed. Health tokens, never the direction pair. */
.panel::before{ content:""; position:absolute; left:0; top:0; bottom:0; width:3px;
  background:var(--accent,var(--info)); transition:background .25s ease; }
html[data-unsub="off"]   .panel{ --accent:var(--ok); }
html[data-unsub="on"]    .panel{ --accent:var(--ok); }
html[data-unsub="bad"]   .panel{ --accent:var(--act); }
html[data-err="1"]       .panel{ --accent:var(--act); }

.p-head{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; padding:13px 18px;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
.p-head .mlab{ flex:1; color:var(--text); }
html[data-unsub="off"] .p-head .mlab{ color:var(--ok); }
.p-body{ padding:18px; }
@media (min-width:600px){ .p-body{ padding:22px 24px 20px; } }

/* one state visible at a time; the page boots in `ready` and the JS decides */
.st{ display:none; }
html[data-unsub="ready"] .st-ready,
html[data-unsub="off"]   .st-off,
html[data-unsub="on"]    .st-on,
html[data-unsub="bad"]   .st-bad{ display:block; }
/* FAILURE IS A SEPARATE AXIS, not a fifth state. `error` used to be a data-unsub VALUE
   that displayed .st-ready, so a failed press overwrote the step the reader was on: press
   "Turn them back on" from `off`, have the server 500, and the panel flipped to the label
   MARKETING EMAIL: ON, the unsubscribe lede, and an "Unsubscribe" button — the inverse of
   what was attempted, on a compliance surface, next to a bar saying "try again". The bar
   now rides on data-err, so the step, the label and the button are all still whatever
   they were and "try again" means what it says. */
.lb{ display:none; }
html[data-unsub="ready"] .lb-ready,
html[data-unsub="on"]    .lb-ready,
html[data-unsub="off"]   .lb-off,
html[data-unsub="bad"]   .lb-bad{ display:inline; }

.lede{ margin:0 0 18px; color:var(--muted); font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.55; max-width:48ch; }

/* ── the seal + the recorded state ────────────────────────────────────────── */
.seal{ width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; display:grid; place-items:center;
  color:var(--ok); background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ok) 13%,transparent);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--ok) 34%,transparent); margin-bottom:14px; }
.seal svg{ width:19px; height:19px; }
.seal.bad{ color:var(--act); background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--act) 12%,transparent);
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--act) 34%,transparent); }
.st h2{ font:700 21px/1.2 var(--font-ui); letter-spacing:-.01em; margin:0 0 8px; }
.st p{ margin:0 0 18px; color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.55; max-width:46ch; }
.st p b.addr{ color:var(--text); font-weight:600; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:13.3px; }
/* keep a fallback address whole — a mid-address break reads as a typo */
.st a[href^="mailto:"]{ white-space:nowrap; }

/* ── action row ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.act{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px; flex-wrap:wrap;
  border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding-top:16px; margin-top:2px; }
.act .note{ font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); flex:1; min-width:180px; line-height:1.4; }
/* gbtn — house glass button (theme.css), -cta variant, no breathing animation */
.btn{ position:relative; overflow:hidden; display:inline-flex; align-items:center;
  justify-content:center; gap:7px; padding:10px 20px; border-radius:11px;
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 45%,var(--gbtn-brd));
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 16%,var(--gbtn-bg)), var(--gbtn-bg));
  -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px) saturate(140%); backdrop-filter:blur(12px) saturate(140%);
  color:var(--text); font:600 13.5px/1 var(--font-ui); letter-spacing:.01em; cursor:pointer;
  box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 var(--gbtn-sheen), 0 1px 2px rgba(3,7,18,.18);
  transition:background .2s ease, border-color .2s ease, transform .16s ease, box-shadow .25s ease; }
.btn:hover{ border-color:var(--info); transform:translateY(-1px);
  box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 var(--gbtn-sheen), 0 8px 24px -10px color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 55%,transparent); }
.btn:active{ transform:translateY(0) scale(.985); }
.btn:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid var(--link); outline-offset:2px; }
.btn::after{ content:""; position:absolute; inset:0; pointer-events:none;
  background:linear-gradient(105deg,transparent 40%,rgba(255,255,255,.13) 50%,transparent 60%);
  transform:translateX(-140%) skewX(-8deg); }
.btn:hover::after{ transform:translateX(140%) skewX(-8deg); transition:transform .55s ease; }
.btn[aria-busy="true"]{ pointer-events:none; opacity:.75; }
/* Turning marketing back on is a SECOND action and never the default: ghost weight,
   smaller, no accent fill. The page must not nudge anyone back onto a list they left. */
.btn-ghost{ background:var(--gbtn-bg); border-color:var(--gbtn-brd); color:var(--muted);
  font-size:12.8px; padding:9px 16px; }
.btn-ghost:hover{ color:var(--text); border-color:var(--gbtn-brd-hover); box-shadow:none;
  transform:none; }

/* ── error bar (interface voice: what happened + what to do) ───────────────── */
.err{ display:none; align-items:flex-start; gap:10px; margin:0 0 16px; padding:12px 14px;
  border-radius:11px; font-size:13.2px; line-height:1.45; color:var(--text);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--act) 45%,var(--line));
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--act) 10%,transparent); }
html[data-err="1"] .err{ display:flex; }
.err .ic{ flex:none; width:16px; height:16px; margin-top:1px; color:var(--act); }
.err .ic svg{ display:block; width:16px; height:16px; }
.err a{ white-space:nowrap; }

/* the refused note — a bounce or a complaint is not lifted from a link */
.refused{ display:none; margin:14px 0 0; padding:10px 12px; border-radius:10px;
  font-size:12.9px; line-height:1.45; color:var(--muted);
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 7%,transparent);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 22%,transparent); }
html[data-refused="1"] .refused{ display:block; }
html[data-refused="1"] .st-off .btn-ghost{ display:none; }
/* The way back needs its OWN token — the footer token authorises `unsubscribe` and
   nothing else — and the server only mints one for the request that actually recorded the
   opt-out. No token, no button: a button that can only 400 is worse than no button. */
html:not([data-undo="1"]) .st-off .btn-ghost{ display:none; }

/* ── footer — landing footer anatomy, colours resolved from theme tokens ───── */
.mx-footer{ border-top:1px solid var(--line); margin-top:52px;
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--panel) 45%,transparent);
  padding:38px 0 30px; color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; }
.mx-footer .f-in{ max-width:1000px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 22px; }
.mx-footer .f-grid{ display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-start;
  gap:30px; flex-wrap:wrap; }
.mx-footer .f-brand .fb-row{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:9px; }
.mx-footer .f-brand .fm{ width:26px; height:26px; border-radius:7px;
  background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--brand-a),var(--brand-c)); display:grid; place-items:center;
  font:800 14px/1 var(--font-ui); color:#fff; }
.mx-footer .f-brand .fn{ font:800 13px/1 var(--font-ui); letter-spacing:.08em; color:var(--text); }
.mx-footer .f-brand .ft{ margin:10px 0 0; color:var(--muted); font-size:12.5px; }
.mx-footer .f-cols{ display:flex; gap:clamp(30px,6vw,84px); }
.mx-footer .f-col p{ margin:0 0 8px; font:700 9px/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em;
  color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 78%,transparent); text-transform:uppercase; }
/* Same recipe as .mlab, so it needs the same CJK fix: 9px mono + .14em tracking with no
   Hanzi in the stack renders 产品 / 资源 through whatever the system picks — a serif on
   some machines — at tracking this file's own comment calls broken spacing. */
html[data-lang="zh"] .mx-footer .f-col p{ font-family:"PingFang SC","Hiragino Sans GB",
  "Microsoft YaHei","Noto Sans CJK SC",var(--font-mono); letter-spacing:.04em; }
.mx-footer .f-col a{ display:block; color:var(--muted); padding:4.5px 0; font-size:13px; }
.mx-footer .f-col a:hover{ color:var(--text); }
.mx-footer .f-bot{ display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;
  gap:12px 18px; flex-wrap:wrap; border-top:1px solid var(--line); margin-top:34px;
  padding-top:18px; font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); }

/* ── mobile ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
@media (max-width:480px){
  .wrap{ padding:14px 14px 52px; }
  .hero{ padding:12px 2px 2px; text-align:left; }
  /* the eyebrow's leading hairline reads as a stray indent once left-aligned */
  .hero .eyebrow{ margin-bottom:12px; }
  .hero .eyebrow::before{ display:none; }
  .hero h1{ margin:0; max-width:none; }
  .hero .sub{ margin:12px 0 0; max-width:none; }
  .panel{ border-radius:14px; margin-top:22px; }
  .p-head{ padding:11px 14px; gap:8px; }
  .p-body{ padding:15px 14px 16px; }
  .act{ gap:10px; }
  .act .btn{ width:100%; order:-1; }
  /* ...but NOT the ghost one. `.act .btn` matches `.btn.btn-ghost` too, so on a phone the
     "turn them back on" button became full width and jumped ABOVE its own note — the
     loudest thing on screen and the only button visible, on the exact surface where email
     links are opened. It is a second, quieter action everywhere or it is not one. */
  .act .btn-ghost{ width:auto; order:0; }
  .act .note{ min-width:0; }
  .mx-footer{ padding:30px 0 24px; margin-top:38px; }
  .mx-footer .f-in{ padding:0 16px; }
  .mx-footer .f-grid{ gap:24px; }
  .mx-footer .f-cols{ gap:40px; }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .btn, .btn::after, .panel::before{ transition:none; }
  .btn:hover{ transform:none; }
}
</style>
